{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Secret scan (pre-commit gate)",
  "description": "Scans staged and recently changed files for secrets before code leaves the working tree. Kiro has no git pre-commit event, so this hook uses two triggers: (1) agentStop — runs automatically whenever Kiro finishes a code-writing session, catching secrets before the developer commits; (2) userTriggered — lets the developer invoke the scan manually at any time. The agentStop trigger is the closest approximation to a pre-commit hook available in Kiro's event model.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "agentStop",
    "patterns": []
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Run a secret scan over all staged files and any files modified since the last commit. Use `git diff --name-only HEAD` and `git diff --name-only --cached` to obtain the file list, then search each file for the following patterns:\n\n- `sk-` (OpenAI secret keys)\n- `AIza` (Google/Firebase API keys)\n- `ghp_` (GitHub personal access tokens)\n- `gho_` (GitHub OAuth tokens)\n- `xox` (Slack tokens: xoxb-, xoxp-, xoxa-, xoxs-)\n- `AKIA` (AWS access key IDs)\n- `-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----`\n- `-----BEGIN EC PRIVATE KEY-----`\n- `-----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----`\n- `-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----`\n\nAllow list (do NOT flag these):\n- The literal string `sk-REDACTED` in test fixture files — this is the approved redacted placeholder.\n\nFor every match outside the allow list:\n1. Report the file path, line number, and the matched pattern (do NOT echo the actual secret value).\n2. Tell the developer to remove the secret, replace it with the approved placeholder if it is a fixture, rotate the credential if it may have been committed previously, and add the file to .gitignore if appropriate.\n3. Do NOT commit, push, or stage any files during this hook.\n\nIf no matches are found outside the allow list, report: 'Secret scan passed — no secrets detected in changed files.'"
  }
}
